---
import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="API Reference | DP-LMI Package">
  <section class="hero compact">
    <h1>API Reference</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      The public reference tracks implemented MATLAB classes and functions.
      Backend behavior is documented only where it explains user-visible
      <code>dpmat</code> and <code>dpvar</code> behavior.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="reference-list" aria-label="API reference index">
    <article id="dpbase" class="reference-item">
      <h2><code>dpbase</code></h2>
      <p>
        Backend parent for grid metadata, cell ordering, local coefficient
        storage, inherited inspection properties, and validation. Ordinary
        modeling code should construct <code>dpmat</code> or <code>dpvar</code>.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article id="dpmat" class="reference-item">
      <h2><code>dpmat</code></h2>
      <p>
        Known finite real matrix data. Supported behavior includes
        coefficient-backed construction, function-backed construction,
        evaluation, display, <code>table</code>, plotting, matrix operations,
        indexing, assignment, <code>isequal</code>, coefficient algebra,
        numeric promotion, common-grid refinement, and zero fast paths.
      </p>
      <pre><code>{`A = dpmat({[0 1]}, {1, 2}, Degree=1);
B = dpmat({[0 1]}, {10, 20, 30}, Degree=2);
C = A + B;
D = A * A;`}</code></pre>
    </article>

    <article id="dpvar" class="reference-item">
      <h2><code>dpvar</code></h2>
      <p>
        YALMIP-backed gridded Bernstein decision expressions. Supported
        behavior includes symmetric/full construction, degree-zero constants,
        affine algebra, compatible numeric and <code>dpmat</code> promotion,
        supported known-data products, matrix operations, comparisons, and
        rate-weighted derivatives through <code>rhodiff</code>.
      </p>
      <pre><code>{`P = dpvar(2, {[0 1]}, "symmetric", RateBounds=[-1 1]);
dP = rhodiff(P);
C = dP + P <= 0;`}</code></pre>
    </article>

    <article id="dplmi" class="reference-item">
      <h2><code>dplmi</code></h2>
      <p>
        Finite YALMIP constraint assembly from <code>dpvar</code> residuals.
        Comparisons such as <code>P >= 0</code> are the primary entry point.
        <code>toYalmip</code> exposes the assembled constraints for ordinary
        YALMIP <code>optimize</code> calls.
      </p>
      <pre><code>{`C = P >= 0;
constraints = C.toYalmip;
sol = optimize(constraints, [], sdpsettings("verbose", 0));`}</code></pre>
    </article>

    <article id="bernsteinTable" class="reference-item">
      <h2><code>bernsteinTable</code></h2>
      <p>
        Returns a tabular view of coefficient-backed object cells, local
        labels, physical grid coordinates, Bernstein basis strings, and stored
        values. <code>dpmat/table</code> delegates to this public helper.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
